Weibull distribution
The Weibull distribution, with shape parameter \(k \in (0, \infty)\) and scale parameter \(\lambda \in (0, + \infty)\). Its pdf is defined as
\[
f(x; \lambda, k) =
\begin{cases}
\frac{k}{\lambda}(\frac{x}{\lambda})^{k-1} e^{-(x/\lambda)^k}, & x \geq 0, \\
0, & x &lt; 0
\end{cases}
\]


